# Site Review stays current

The KPF live site review is the canvas
`/Users/daneoleary/.cursor/projects/Users-daneoleary-Documents-Work-Kevin-Popke-Foundation/canvases/kpf-live-site-review.canvas.tsx`.

After any prompt that ships, fixes, or verifies something on the public site, DreamHost CMS, Faust/wp-env pins, GraphQL, performance, a11y, or security:

1. Open that canvas and update it in the same turn — do not wait to be asked.
2. Mark matching `OPEN` todos `completed` (or `cancelled` if dropped). Add a `COMPLETED` row with the date and what actually went live.
3. Remove or rewrite `PROBLEMS` / `IMPLEMENT` / `WP_CONFLICTS` / Sequence / callouts so they match live + git, not the old snapshot.
4. Skip the canvas for work that does not change the review (copy-only chat, unrelated files, masters/, local-only experiments that never ship).
5. When you mention the canvas, link the `.canvas.tsx` file.

Never dump the review as a chat markdown table instead of updating the canvas.
